  "verified_mechanisms": [
    "One existing opaque CAMetalLayer now covers address, heading, New Tab and list. Rust aligns fixed controls with the actual list viewport; the native scrollbar gutter remains outside the canvas.",
    "The address pill inherits the existing Rust row pointer/key reducer and application OpenAddress(false) callback. Metal creates no host/path Labels. Native system font metrics feed Rust adjacent host/path geometry, with a bold host and tail-elided path.",
    "Rust emits address fill, outline, search/lock icon and focus indicator. Analytic inset strokes use the existing 32-byte GPU quad ABI, with frame fingerprints including stroke width. No third-party icon/font/crate dependency was added.",
    "The workspace heading stores its text directly, exposes one native static-text accessibility node and emits inset bold Unicode/emoji scene text. Views retains its ordinary Label backend.",
    "The address native accessibility node retains its action/name and explicitly describes the displayed host/path. Native painting is absent while Metal owns the control and returns when the panel is hidden.",
    "Browser regressions physically click the address pill, check the full current URL in the existing editor, invoke native main-window Cmd+L, navigate an intercepted HTTPS URL, resize to 200/480, wait for new dark/light submissions and switch workspaces with distinct emoji headings.",
    "Ownership, animation, swipe and drawable-failure paths invalidate fixed control fallback records. Fractional viewport and New Tab canvas-origin assertions remain valid with the extended top region.",
    "The full Metal matrix covers live tabs, native mouse/drag/close, scrolling, split/pin/folders, persistence, workspace swipes, palettes, settings and large-sidebar cache invariants. Views controls were expanded for the shared address refactor."
  ],
  "test_corrections": [
    "An initial assertion incorrectly required a Button to have no children; Chromium installs a native focus-ring child. It now recursively verifies the actual requirement: no hidden native text Labels.",
    "An initial keyboard check tried to focus the intentionally nonactivating sidebar panel and timed out. The final regression exercises existing native main-window Cmd+L instead, preserving Views keyboard semantics. Physical pointer activation and editor URL assertions remain unchanged."
  ],
  "manual_observations": [
    "The matching signed app showed a readable address host/path, analytic search icon, workspace heading, New Tab and the original Unicode split pair.",
    "Clicking the address pill opened the existing palette with the full current URL selected.",
    "Switching to the isolated personal workspace updated the fixed heading. Cmd+L selected its distinct current page URL. Switching back restored the original split pair and heading.",
    "The prototype was closed; its launcher exited successfully. The normal application/profile was not used."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Native outer vertical placement, Button/View event and accessibility nodes, nonactivating panel policy, address editing/IME and browser commands remain adapters. This is not complete Views container removal.",
    "Navigation/footer controls, resize/autohide state, split headers/divider, native animation snapshots and the remaining palettes/forms still need migration.",
    "AX metadata checks and manual UI observations are not a complete VoiceOver/IME/scale matrix.",
    "Submitted command counts and browser test durations do not measure CPU/GPU completion or physical presentation speedup. A controlled real-workload comparison remains required.",
    "No new third-party binary dependency was introduced; upstream notices and existing Apache-2.0 original-code licensing remain unchanged."
